          "heading": "Unit project and experiment",
          "content": "## Unit project and experiment\n\n\n\nA classroom floor includes two 6 m spans and a 300\u00d7550 mm downstand beam. Prepare a free-body diagram for each construction stage and the final supported system. Use a preliminary 4 kN/m\u00b2 permanent floor load, a distinct beam self-weight estimate and a 3 kN/m\u00b2 imposed floor load on a 3 m tributary strip. Compare a conservative simply supported model with a continuous-beam elastic model. Document which one predicts top reinforcement near the interior support. Select a trial f\u2032c and fy and establish both nominal and code-based design checks without silently mixing load factors. Draw reinforcement continuity, anchorage and stirrup zones. Include a serviceability assessment and at least one sensitivity to effective depth. Submit a list of missing information rather than assuming you can authorize construction.\n\n\n\n**Deliverable:** A transparent engineering memo with assumptions, diagrams, units, hand-checks, source references and a list of issues that need a governing-code and professional review."
