          "secNumber": "2.8",
          "heading": "Unit project and experiment",
          "content": "## Unit project and experiment\n\n\n\nCompare two beam sections constrained to a 300\u00d7550 mm gross rectangle: a singly reinforced section and a doubly reinforced section. Choose concrete strength, steel strength, nominal cover and bar diameters. For each layout draw the concrete compression block and strain distribution for a positive bending case, solve force equilibrium, calculate nominal moment and state the strain assumption. Check geometric fit with the reinforcement-cage lab. Discuss the cost of steel quantity, congestion and long-term serviceability. Test a higher-grade steel option and explain why greater fy does not automatically improve ductility or bond. End with a transparent checklist of design-code checks still missing from the simplified calculations.\n\n\n\n**Deliverable:** A transparent engineering memo with assumptions, diagrams, units, hand-checks, source references and a list of issues that need a governing-code and professional review."
