          "heading": "Unit project and experiment",
          "content": "## Unit project and experiment\n\n\n\nAnalyze a 6\u00d76 m flat slab panel supported at four columns, with an opening near one column and a specified imposed load. Prepare a plan with column strip and middle strip candidates. Discuss alternative two-way analysis methods and why unsupported bending-strip allocations are not trustworthy. Calculate gravity load totals and a first-pass concentric punching stress for an unperforated interior-column case, then sketch the truncated perimeter caused by the opening and discuss altered demand. Indicate top steel areas near column regions and bottom steel zones only after selecting an appropriate code model. Add serviceability, fire, progressive-collapse integrity and construction-stage considerations. Present a drawing with noted uncertainties.\n\n\n\n**Deliverable:** A transparent engineering memo with assumptions, diagrams, units, hand-checks, source references and a list of issues that need a governing-code and professional review."
