          "secNumber": "6.8",
          "heading": "Unit project and experiment",
          "content": "## Unit project and experiment\n\n\n\nA 1200 kN column reaction acts on a preliminary square isolated footing. For candidate widths of 2.4, 2.8 and 3.2 m, calculate uniform bearing pressures under a centered-load assumption. For each width, estimate cantilever moments and the net punching demand around a 450 mm square column with stated effective depth. Plot pressure and punching stress against width and explain why enlarging the plan is not a substitute for depth or reinforcement verification. Add footing and soil self-weight to a revised model, and create a separate eccentric-load sketch. Propose what the geotechnical consultant must provide: allowable or design bearing resistance, settlement, groundwater, excavation and construction constraints.\n\n\n\n**Deliverable:** A transparent engineering memo with assumptions, diagrams, units, hand-checks, source references and a list of issues that need a governing-code and professional review."
