          "secNumber": "7.8",
          "heading": "Unit project and experiment",
          "content": "## Unit project and experiment\n\n\n\nA reinforced concrete floor shows visible cracks and increasing sag after occupancy. Build competing hypotheses: under-reinforcement, excessive construction loading, shrinkage restraint, poor curing, creep, inadequate anchorage, or differential support movement. For each hypothesis identify one observation or test that would increase or decrease its plausibility. Reconstruct the as-built reinforcement depth and cover from reliable evidence rather than assuming drawings are exact. Compute simple uncracked and cracked stiffness estimates and document their limitations. Use the cracking and deflection labs to explore sensitivity. Present an investigation plan distinguishing non-destructive screening, intrusive inspection and an engineer-supervised structural assessment; do not declare the floor safe from simulation results.\n\n\n\n**Deliverable:** A transparent engineering memo with assumptions, diagrams, units, hand-checks, source references and a list of issues that need a governing-code and professional review."
