          "id": "sec-8-8",
          "secNumber": "8.8",
          "heading": "Unit project and experiment",
          "content": "## Unit project and experiment\n\n\n\nPrepare a 50-year exposure and maintenance concept for a coastal building component. Identify likely transport mechanisms, wetting and drying patterns, cover quality, cracking risk and inspection access. Compare a carbonation-front surrogate with a chloride-focused conceptual assessment; make explicit that the two models address different chemistry and cannot be interchanged. Select a preliminary cementitious-material strategy and explain curing, cover, drainage and protective details. Define a verification matrix tying each design assumption to a source, calculation, test or inspection. Include a change-control log showing how a revised exposure class, changed bar grade or moved construction joint would trigger new engineering review. Submit a record of assumptions that require local code and professional approval.\n\n\n\n**Deliverable:** A transparent engineering memo with assumptions, diagrams, units, hand-checks, source references and a list of issues that need a governing-code and professional review."
